  "_doc": {
    "purpose": "Canonical metro_id ↔ display_name ↔ MSA/county/zillow lookup. Built for merge into Masmedeam/groundswell (Salim's repo), whose ES indices key on metro_id. His demo set (sf/austin/phoenix/nyc/chicago) is a subset of these 17; same metro_id strings are used here so joins are zero-friction.",
    "id_convention": "lowercase city for single-word metros; initialism for multi-word (matches Salim's existing convention: sf, nyc). Optional aliases listed when an alternate is common (e.g. dfw for Dallas, atl for Atlanta) — Salim/I can pick whichever feels right when we merge.",
    "use_for_joining": "Every signal row in data/*.json (employment, rent, warn, postings, jolts, permits, wages, rent-vs-own, zhvi) carries a `metro` field with the display_name. Use name_lookups.by_display_name to translate to metro_id at load time."
